equate levels of this essential vitamin, which is necessary for the proper functioning of the coagulation process in the body.", "D3:", "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PAEDIATRIC GASTROENTEROLOGY, HEPATOLOGY, AND NUTRITION:A professional organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for pediatric nutrition, particularly for preterm infants.", "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF PAEDIATRIC RESEARCH:A society that promotes research in pediatric health and nutrition, supporting studies and guidelines for better health outcomes in children.", "J PEDIATR GASTROENTEROL NUTR:The \"J PEDIATR GASTROENTEROL NUTR,\" also known as the Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition, is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research and guidelines pertinent to the fields of pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. The journal features a variety of studies, including those focused on pediatric gastrointestinal health and specific conditions such as cystic fibrosis. It serves as a vital resource for professionals in the field, contributing to the advancement of knowledge and practices related to the nutritional and gastrointestinal well-being of children.", "NUTRITIONAL NEEDS OF THE PRETERM INFANT:A guideline published by the American Academy of Pediatrics addressing the specific nutritional requirements for preterm infants.", "HILLTOP TRIAL:A randomized controlled trial investigating the use of heparin in total parenteral nutrition to prevent sepsis in neonates.", "NUTRITION OF THE PRETERM INFANT:A comprehensive overview of the nutritional requirements and guidelines for preterm infants.", "BUONOCORE G:Buonocore G is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr.", "CARNIELLI VP:Carnelli VP is a co-author of a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants published in J Pediatr Gastroenterol Nutr.", "DE CURTIS M:De Curtis M is a prominent researcher in the field of neonatal nutrition, particularly focusing on the nutritional needs of preterm infants. They have co-authored a commentary on enteral nutrient supply for preterm infants, which was published in the Journal of Pediatric Gastroenterology and Nutrition. Additionally, De Curtis M contributed to a document addressing the nutrition of preterm infants, published in Early Human Development. Their research also encompasses the study of parenteral nutrition in premature infants, highlighting their commitment to improving nutritional strategies for this vulnerable population."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}